abstract: >-
  For the SU(2) Wilson lattice gauge theory on Z^4, the gap of the one-step transfer operator tends to zero as beta tends to infinity,
  for every family of translation-invariant Gibbs states that are reflection positive for the time reflection through a hyperplane of sites
  (limsup of the gap <= B(t) = (2/t) log(c(0)/c(t)), c an explicit free Maxwell correlation; same bound in the gauge-invariant sector and after removal
  of the eigenspaces at +1 and -1). Explicit power-law rate m <= 24 beta^(-1/120) log beta for beta >= 1e228 (smaller than 1 only beyond beta ~ 1e455); no exponential rate, no confinement statement, no continuum mass gap; neither assertion of Problem 5.1 of Chatterjee
  is proved; historical novelty not established. Not refereed; no human has checked the proofs.
